Description: cham3 KDE Plasma 6 Wayland desktop defaults (M1 visual foundation)
 Installs the cham3 desktop customization for KDE Plasma 6 on Wayland: a dark
 color scheme, the cham3 wallpaper and logos, a look-and-feel package that
 defaults to a vertical panel on the right screen edge, and eight Plasma
 widgets (plasmoids) for that panel. It depends on the Debian KDE Plasma
 session and the KDE core utilities (Dolphin, Konsole, Kate, Ark, Okular,
 Gwenview, Spectacle and Plasma System Monitor).
 .
 This is a visual and package foundation only. The cham3 panel widgets are
 inert: they render their layout and report every backend-dependent feature
 (identity, alias and tag services, contracts, network protocol editor, Full
 Isolation Kill, task attribution) as unavailable. Installing this package does
 not provide application isolation, permission contracts, network mode
 enforcement or a kill switch, and a widget on screen is not evidence that any
 security policy is active.
 .
 Packet capture: cham3-desktop keeps /usr/bin/dumpcap, which wireshark-common
 ships, out of set-user-id root. Its preinst registers a dpkg-statoverride on
 the file before wireshark-common can be configured, and its postinst and a
 dpkg file trigger keep it root:wireshark, mode 0750, with only the
 cap_net_admin and cap_net_raw file capabilities. If those
 capabilities cannot be set, capture by non-root users is unavailable; the
 set-user-id fallback of wireshark-common is never used. Installing the
 package adds no user to the wireshark group: membership is a deliberate
 per-user administrative step that lets that user capture packets.
